{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":30000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"b4db04a51df0d26829633310bc3b4f4461e88399a33584f192478cafce9d84df","packTokens":9128,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":255,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":528,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":705,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":1692,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":341,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":5492,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":7,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"critic"},"pointers":[],"system":"Adversarial reviewer. Find defects in this spec; don't praise; don't rewrite it.\nRubric: 1 conflicts between requirements 2 missing error, empty and permission paths 3 ACs not observable at a public surface 4 scope creep beyond the intent 5 claims about existing behaviour without anchors 6 state transitions and existing data 7 behaviour changes outside the requested scope (blast radius) 8 hardcoded identifiers that should be configuration.\nEach finding: rubric number, reqId, severity (critical|high|medium|low), one-sentence evidence in \"finding\". Empty list if none.\nThe human answered questions and accepted assumptions (below). Scope they decided is not a defect: don't flag it.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"intent\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"changeClass\": \"feature\",\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-30T20:46:31.819Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"intent\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n   \"stage\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20260930-invoice-reminders-a-small-4006\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"rigor\": \"full\",\n \"risk\": \"high\",\n \"riskTags\": [\n  \"public-api\",\n  \"auth\",\n  \"payments\",\n  \"pii\"\n ],\n \"source\": \"cli\",\n \"spans\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-1\",\n   \"text\": \"When an invoice is 7 days past its due date, the system shall mark it overdue and show it on the overdue list\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-2\",\n   \"text\": \"When staff press 'Send reminder' on an overdue invoice, the system shall email the customer a reminder with the invoice number, amount and due date\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-3\",\n   \"text\": \"The system shall record each reminder sent, with who sent it and when, and show the history on the invoice\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-4\",\n   \"text\": \"If an email cannot be delivered, the system shall show the failure on the invoice and keep it on the overdue list\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-5\",\n   \"text\": \"Staff shall be able to filter the overdue list by customer and by days overdue\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-6\",\n   \"text\": \"Build overdue list screen (table, filters, a 'Send reminder' button per row)\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-7\",\n   \"text\": \"Build invoice detail screen (amount, due date, reminder history, delivery failures)\"\n  }\n ],\n \"touchesUi\": true\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who can view the screens and send reminders, and how do staff sign in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any authenticated staff user, using the existing API's authentication\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which email address receives the reminder, and what happens if the customer has several contacts or none?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The customer's single billing email from the existing record; if missing, the send is blocked with an error\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Can reminder history entries be edited or deleted?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No, they are append-only and immutable\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Payments are out of scope. So how does an invoice come off the overdue list once it is paid or closed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The existing system's invoice status (paid/cancelled) is read and closed invoices drop off automatically\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should repeated sends be guarded against?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Disable the button while a send is in progress only\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Is 'overdue' a status saved on the invoice (for example by a daily job), or is it worked out from the due date each time the list loads?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Computed at query time from due date and today's date\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Where are reminder history records stored, given that invoices live in the client's existing system?\",\n  \"answer\": \"New table in the same Postgres database, referencing invoice ID\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Is a failed send recorded in the append-only reminder history, and does a later successful send clear the failure shown on the invoice?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Every attempt (success or failure) is a history entry; the latest status is shown\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-1\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Where do invoices and customers come from? Are they already stored in the client's existing .NET 8 API / Postgres database, or does this app create and own them? → assumed: Invoices and customers already exist in the client's API/database; this app reads them and adds overdue and reminder data\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-2\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the 7-day overdue threshold be fixed in code or a configuration setting? And how are days counted (calendar days, in which time zone)? → assumed: Configurable setting, default 7 calendar days, business time zone\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-3\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What does 'days overdue' mean in the list and its filter: days since the due date, or days since the invoice was marked overdue (due date + 7)? → assumed: Days since the due date\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-4\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should the days-overdue filter work? → assumed: Preset buckets (7–30, 31–60, 60+)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-5\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Which email service sends reminders, and how is 'cannot be delivered' detected? → assumed: Transactional email provider (e.g. SendGrid/Postmark) with bounce webhooks; both send errors and later bounces count as failures\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-6\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Does a send attempt that fails at once (e.g. provider error, no email) still create a reminder history entry? → assumed: Yes, every attempt is logged with its outcome (sent/failed/bounced)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-7\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Can staff open the invoice detail screen from the overdue list? → assumed: Yes, clicking the invoice number or row opens the detail screen\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-8\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the invoice detail screen also have a 'Send reminder' button for overdue invoices? → assumed: Yes, when the invoice is overdue\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-9\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Does the reminder email need a specific template, sender name/address, or currency format? → assumed: A simple fixed template from a configured sender address, amounts in GBP/local currency\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-10\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the 7-day overdue threshold be a fixed constant or a setting that can be changed? → assumed: Configurable setting, defaulting to 7 days\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-11\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which date and timezone decide when an invoice is '7 days past due', and is 'days overdue' (used in the filter) counted from the due date or from when the invoice became overdue? → assumed: Calendar days in the business's local timezone, counted from the due date\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-12\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which email service sends the reminders, and what sender address should they come from? → assumed: To be decided; abstract behind an interface with SMTP default\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-13\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What counts as 'cannot be delivered': only errors when the email is handed to the mail service, or also later bounces and rejections? → assumed: Only immediate send errors from the mail service\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-14\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the invoice detail screen also have a 'Send reminder' button when the invoice is overdue? → assumed: Yes, same action and in-progress disabling as the list\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-15\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What wording and format should the reminder email use, and should the amount show a currency symbol? → assumed: Fixed plain template with invoice number, amount in local currency, due date\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-30T20:46:31.847Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20260930-invoice-reminders-a-small-4006\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": [\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-1\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-5\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-6\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-7\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice reminders system shall classify an invoice as overdue, working this out on every request and never storing it, only when its status in the existing system is in the configured open-status list (default ['open']), it has a due date, and the number of calendar days from its due date to today's date, both taken in the configured business time zone, is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7).\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-10\",\n    \"ASM-11\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold is the default 7, business time zone Europe/London, the injected clock set to 2026-10-15, and open invoices due 2026-10-08 and 2026-10-09\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice\",\n     \"then\": \"the call for the invoice due 2026-10-08 returns overdue = true and daysOverdue = 7, and the call for the invoice due 2026-10-09 returns overdue = false and daysOverdue = 6\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold set to 10, today 2026-10-15, and open invoices due 2026-10-07, 2026-10-06 and 2026-10-05\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice\",\n     \"then\": \"the calls return overdue = false for the invoices due 2026-10-07 and 2026-10-06, and overdue = true for the invoice due 2026-10-05\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.3\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold 7, default open-status list ['open'], and seven invoices each 20 days past due with statuses paid, cancelled, draft, void, written-off, disputed and credited\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice\",\n     \"then\": \"every call returns overdue = false\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.4\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold 7 and an invoice with status 'open' and a null due date\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for it\",\n     \"then\": \"the call returns overdue = false and throws no exception\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.5\",\n     \"given\": \"business time zone Europe/London, default threshold, and an open invoice due 2026-09-01\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called at instant 2026-09-07T22:30Z (23:30 on 7 Sep local), then at 2026-09-07T23:30Z (00:30 on 8 Sep local)\",\n     \"then\": \"the first call returns daysOverdue = 6 and overdue = false, and the second returns daysOverdue = 7 and overdue = true\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.6\",\n     \"given\": \"an open invoice due 6 days ago is not in the overdue list response, and no job or data change runs\",\n     \"when\": \"the injected clock moves forward 1 day and the overdue list is requested again\",\n     \"then\": \"the response now holds the invoice with daysOverdue = 7, and the invoice record in the existing database is unchanged\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the Invoice Reminders API shall return every invoice currently classified as overdue, each with invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue (calendar days since the due date).\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-3\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"given\": \"today 2026-10-15, threshold 7, and in the existing database: open invoice A for customer 'Crumb & Co' with amount 125.50 due 2026-10-01, open invoice B due 2026-10-12, invoice C due 2026-09-01 with status paid, and invoice D due 2026-09-01 with status cancelled\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 200 and holds only invoice A, with its invoice number, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 125.50, due date 2026-10-01 and daysOverdue 14\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"given\": \"invoice A is in the overdue list\",\n     \"when\": \"its status in the existing system is changed to paid and the overdue list is requested again\",\n     \"then\": \"invoice A is no longer in the response and no overdue flag was written to the invoice record\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only the overdue invoices that belong to that customer.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"given\": \"customer X has 2 overdue invoices, customer Y has 1 overdue invoice, and customer Z has none\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list with customerId = X, then with customerId = Z\",\n     \"then\": \"the first response holds exactly customer X's 2 invoices and the second response is 200 with an empty list\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall inside the named fixed bucket (7–30, 31–60 or 61+, limits inclusive, not shifted by the configured overdue threshold), or respond 400 with a validation error when the bucket value is not one of these.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-3\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"given\": \"default threshold 7 and overdue invoices at 7, 30, 31, 60, 61 and 90 days overdue\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with bucket 7–30, then 31–60, then 61+\",\n     \"then\": \"the responses hold {7, 30}, {31, 60} and {61, 90}\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"given\": \"customers X and Y each have overdue invoices at 10 and 45 days\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with customerId = X and bucket 31–60, then with customerId = X and bucket 7–30\",\n     \"then\": \"the first response holds only X's 45-day invoice and the second holds only X's 10-day invoice\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n     \"given\": \"any overdue invoices\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with an unknown bucket value such as '5-6'\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 400 with a validation error naming the bucket parameter\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.4\",\n     \"given\": \"the overdue threshold is set to 5 and an open invoice is 6 days past due\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested without a bucket, then with bucket 7–30, 31–60 and 61+\",\n     \"then\": \"the invoice is in the unfiltered response and is in none of the three bucket responses\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint has no valid staff authentication from the existing API, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data, sending email or changing data.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"given\": \"no token, and separately an expired token\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list endpoint is called, with and without customer and bucket filters\",\n     \"then\": \"each response is 401 with no invoice or customer data in the body\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n     \"given\": \"a valid token for any staff user with no special role\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list endpoint is called\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 200, not 401 or 403\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint carries a valid, unexpired token from the existing API whose principal is not a staff user, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 403 without returning invoice or customer data or changing data.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"given\": \"a valid, unexpired token issued by the existing API for a principal without the staff marker (for example a service/integration client or a non-staff user account)\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list endpoint is called, with and without customer and bucket filters\",\n     \"then\": \"each response is 403 and its body holds no invoice or customer data\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"text\": \"The overdue list endpoint meets the stated latency at the stated data volumes, with or without filters.\",\n   \"metric\": \"p95 ≤ 1,000 ms at the API with 10,000 invoices (at least 5,000 of them open), with or without filters\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"text\": \"Customer PII (billing email addresses) and invoice amounts are kept out of application logs.\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 customer billing email addresses found in application log output across the whole automated acceptance test run\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"text\": \"All Invoice Reminders endpoints require staff authentication.\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of new Invoice Reminders endpoints return 401 without a valid token and 403 with a valid non-staff token (checked by an automated endpoint sweep)\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Run 2 of the sequence (not this run): sending a reminder email for an overdue invoice (I-2), recording append-only reminder history with sender and time (I-3, Q-3, Q-7, Q-8), recording and showing send failures (I-4, ASM-13), the invoice detail API with history (I-7), rejecting sends for non-overdue, missing-billing-email and unknown invoices, and adding the latest reminder outcome to the overdue list items; see suggestions for the moved requirements REQ-7 to REQ-13 and REQ-18\",\n  \"Run 3 of the sequence (not this run): building the React overdue list screen (table, customer and bucket filters, per-row 'Send reminder' button, link to detail) and invoice detail screen (amount, due date, history, failures, 'Send reminder' button while overdue) described in I-6 and I-7; this run delivers only the overdue list API those screens use\",\n  \"Run 3 of the sequence (not this run): disabling the 'Send reminder' button while a send is in progress (Q-5, ASM-14) and showing the send result on screen\",\n  \"Payments and recording payments (paid/cancelled status is only read from the existing system)\",\n  \"Customer logins or any customer-facing screens\",\n  \"SMS reminders\",\n  \"Detecting delivery failures after hand-off (bounces, complaint/provider webhooks, later rejections); only immediate email-sender errors count as failures (ASM-13)\",\n  \"Automatic or scheduled reminders; every send is started by staff\",\n  \"A stored 'overdue' status on the invoice or a daily job to set it; overdue is computed at query time (Q-6)\",\n  \"Server-side duplicate-send protection (cooldown, daily limit, duplicate check) (Q-5)\",\n  \"Role-based permissions beyond 'any authenticated staff user' (Q-1)\",\n  \"Creating or editing invoices, customers or billing emails (ASM-1)\",\n  \"Sending to more than one contact per customer (Q-2)\",\n  \"Editing or deleting reminder history entries (Q-3)\",\n  \"Configurable email templates or wording (ASM-9, ASM-15)\",\n  \"Days-overdue buckets that move with the configured threshold; buckets are fixed at 7–30, 31–60, 61+\"\n ],\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"Run sequence: the spec was still over the feature size budget, so the work is split into three runs. Run 1 (this spec) covers the read side of the API: overdue rule, overdue list, customer and bucket filters, and authentication (REQ-1, REQ-2, REQ-3, REQ-4, REQ-14, REQ-19). Run 2 covers sending, reminder history, failures, invoice detail and unknown-invoice handling (old REQ-7 to REQ-13, REQ-18, plus the latest reminder outcome on list items, old AC-2.3). Run 3 covers the React screens. Run 2 and Run 3 requirements are kept under suggestions.\",\n  \"REQ-2 no longer returns 'latest reminder outcome' in this run, because the reminder history table it reads from is built in Run 2. Run 2 adds the field back (old AC-2.3).\",\n  \"Staff vs non-staff: a staff user is a principal whose existing-API token carries the staff marker (a claim or role such as user type = staff; the exact claim must be confirmed against the client's auth before build). Any other principal with a valid token (service or integration clients, non-staff user accounts) is non-staff and gets 403. No token, an expired token or an invalid token gets 401.\",\n  \"The bucket conflict is settled in favour of fixed buckets (old REQ-5, 2 of 3 drafts, matches ASM-4's literal 7–30 / 31–60 / 60+). The rule is part of REQ-4 (AC-4.4). Old REQ-6 (lowest bucket starts at the threshold) is dropped. If the threshold is set below 7, invoices overdue by fewer than 7 days appear only in the unfiltered list.\",\n  \"The existing .NET 8 API / Postgres schema was not available to check (current-behaviour: 'no repository: this is new build work'). These are logical fields that must be mapped to the client's real schema and confirmed before build: invoice status values (open, paid, cancelled and others), customer name, invoice number and amount fields, and the token claims that hold the staff user ID and staff marker. Test data is seeded through the confirmed schema.\",\n  \"An invoice can be overdue only if its existing-system status is in a configured open-status allow-list (default ['open'], to be confirmed against the client's status values). Any other status (paid, cancelled, draft, void, written-off, disputed, credited, or unknown) and any null due date is never overdue. 